adjudication.rationale:
The handler authorizes the webhook based on:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is **unset** (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET === undefined`) and the request also omits the header (`req.headers[...] === undefined`), then the comparison is `undefined !== undefined` which is false, so the request passes the secret check and proceeds to create/update credentials. This is a fail-open auth gate when the secret is unconfigured, enabling unauthenticated writes (subject to `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` being true).
